{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261025-deb2","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-25T00:00:00Z","claim":"Requirement 2 is unmet for a colon heading: slice_heading_index matches group(1).rstrip(':') while the records component names the slice group(1).strip() with no colon strip (legacy.py:219), so `## Slice A:` is slice A to signoff-v2 and slice A: to the records component. Requirement 3 (a heading with no separator reads as today) pulls the other way, so the spec conflicts with itself for this shape.","finding":"f1:088f8a6c79a4c462a927","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-25-e18-one-command-loop.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/ledger.py","line":113,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/ledger.py:113","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"86d320738190ee13e071ddef02ee152b738b6c8fb5d0edf34ed37dc64f679b40","raised_by":"A","scenario":"A build doc with `## Slice A:` (or `## Slice A: - x`) and a Status line: ledger.card_of(text, 'A') returns ('built', 4) and set_card moves that card, while legacy.parse_document names the slice 'A:' and card_of(text, 'A:') returns (None, None); the card signoff-v2 sets and the records it appends name different slices. The spec, correctness and seams reviewers' probes and the session's own probe all print records name 'A:' against ledger name 'A'.","seq":8,"severity":"MAJOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"a2b1cd98436c38f30b4c68d422696db01288d43f","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261025-deb2","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-25T00:00:00Z","claim":"The widened SLICE_HEADING and RECORD_HEADING patterns now match hyphen and en dash headings inside fenced code blocks, which the records component skips (FENCE_RE, legacy.py:194-205). slice_heading_index, card_of, set_card and ledger_home have no fence awareness, so a fenced example heading placed before the real one now wins. The base ledger read only the em dash and ignored such a fenced example.","finding":"f1:3ddcf83c3eb5651de1a7","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-25-e18-one-command-loop.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/ledger.py","line":111,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/ledger.py:111","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"3360ae56693cb8bb179976cb3c176225e378c6ca9b0551fa060b20d5aef2b525","raised_by":"A","scenario":"A plan with a fence holding `## Slice A - example` and `Status: not started` above the real `## Slice A <em dash> alpha` and `Status: built`: the new ledger's card_of returns ('not started', 6), the base ledger returned ('built', 11) and the records component reads line 11. set_card writes the verdict inside the fence and the real card stays built while the component's card_set event says otherwise. A fenced `### <date> - review: A` likewise moves ledger_home. No tracked file holds this shape today.","seq":9,"severity":"MAJOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"a2b1cd98436c38f30b4c68d422696db01288d43f","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
{"actor":{"harness":"claude-code","run_id":"signoff-a-20261025-deb2","station":"signoff-v2"},"at":"2026-10-25T00:00:00Z","claim":"A third slice name changes that the spec's 'two names change' does not declare: a dash with no space before it and a space after (`## Slice A<em dash> alpha`, `## Slice A- alpha`) read A before and now reads the whole run, matching the records component but not build-v2's doc.py:36.","finding":"f1:9bd7d4174f71d2f82aa6","kind":"finding_raised","ledger_doc":"docs/plans/2026-10-25-e18-one-command-loop.md","location":{"file":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/ledger.py","line":32,"line_end":null,"more":[],"raw":"plugins/signoff-v2/skills/signoff-v2/scripts/signoff_core/ledger.py:32","resolved":true,"tag":null},"origin":{"kind":"native"},"prev":"30a303451f60c9198674d4aac4729c61d324d20d425765fd894261c727de5c11","raised_by":"A","scenario":"build-v2 reads slice A and moves its card; signoff-v2 then runs on slice A, the full review runs, and set_card raises DocumentShape because card_of(text, 'A') is (None, None). No tracked file holds the shape (seams sweep of 474 files, 0 hits).","seq":10,"severity":"MINOR","slice":"A","source":{"identity":{"commit":"a2b1cd98436c38f30b4c68d422696db01288d43f","dirty":false,"submodules":[],"tracked_diff_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855","untracked":[],"untracked_sha256":"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"},"known":true},"v":1}
